  "notes": "FILED ON BOTH TRIGGERS (delta -14.0, and band crossing Established to Functional). RECOMMENDATION IS flag-for-review, NOT downgrade. CONFIDENCE IS LOW. DO NOT APPLY WITHOUT A TARGETED EVIDENCE PASS. NO ADVERSE EVIDENCE OF ANY KIND WAS FOUND — no labour dispute, regulatory finding, litigation or independent adverse determination. The movement is a 22-company seed-placeholder correction plus the absence-of-disclosure convention, which scores 7 of 40 subdimensions at the low anchor. ManpowerGroup lands at 46.9, the HIGHEST of the five rotation entities this cycle and above the three 60.9-cluster companies de-seeded on 2026-08-18 (HP Inc. 42.5, Marriott 44.4, MetLife 33.1). That ordering is deliberate and defensible: ManpowerGroup carries 17 Ethisphere World's Most Ethical Companies recognitions, a fifth-edition annual sustainability report, and a core business strategy (upskilling and employability) that is genuinely root-cause rather than symptomatic — the strongest Systemic Thinking profile in the batch, and the only subdimension scored at 4/5. SECTOR CAVEAT STATED FOR BALANCE: ManpowerGroup is a staffing company whose model places workers in contingent roles structurally associated with lower security. No independent evidence was located either establishing harm from this or measuring placed-worker outcomes. RECOMMEND A TARGETED PASS on exactly that: independent placed-worker outcome data, wage and benefit levels for placed workers, any national labour-inspectorate findings, and internal turnover data.",
